---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { product } from "../data/product";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms · unottr"
  description="The terms that apply when you buy and use an unottr desktop license."
  eyebrow="License terms"
  heading="A license for your work, not your meeting data."
  intro={`These terms apply to purchases and use of the unottr ${product.licenseVersion} desktop application.`}
>
  <h2>Your license</h2>
  <p>A purchase grants one person a non-exclusive, non-transferable license to install and use unottr for personal and commercial work. The license covers releases in the {product.licenseVersion} version line. A future major version may require a separate purchase.</p>

  <h2>Restrictions</h2>
  <p>You may not redistribute, resell, sublicense, publish, or provide copies of unottr to other people. You may not remove product notices or use the software to build a competing copy. Rights granted by applicable law remain unaffected.</p>

  <h2>Your recordings</h2>
  <p>You keep ownership of your recordings, transcripts, and other content. You are responsible for having permission to record, transcribe, and process a conversation. Recording and consent rules vary by location.</p>

  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>Optional AI connections use services or software you choose. Their fees, terms, output, availability, and data handling are separate from your unottr license. unottr does not guarantee the accuracy of generated answers.</p>

  <h2>Updates and availability</h2>
  <p>The license lets you keep using the version you received. Maintenance updates may change features or supported systems. No software can be promised to work with every future operating system, model provider, or hardware configuration.</p>

  <h2>Warranty and liability</h2>
  <p>unottr is provided as available without a promise that it will be error-free or fit every use. To the extent the law allows, liability is limited to the amount paid for the license. Consumer rights that cannot legally be excluded still apply.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>Updated terms apply to future purchases and product use after their effective date. A material change will be presented on this page before it takes effect.</p>
</LegalLayout>
